// The one HP pool every crew station of every tank shares. Read by
// `src/ballistics/box_classes.rs`, embedded and parsed once, validated at parse.
//
// A crew station's pool is `crew_hp`, filled in when a tank file is parsed; a tank file that
// authors `hp` on a crew-facet volume does not load (`src/spec.rs`). Every other pool is the plain
// `hp` its tank file authors (`<tank>.tank.ron`'s `volumes`), and no rule ties it to the box's
// size. The law is design doc §6, `.agents/docs/design/armor-penetration-and-damage.md`.
//
// The pen cam's potency bands part at `crew_hp` and the least share of an HP point the sim's
// rounding counts, each over the struck tank's crew box face, read from its sim geometry and
// authored nowhere here. Design doc §5, "Potency colour".
//
// PROVENANCE: every value is authored `(value, Kind("source or reason"))`, Kind one of Measured,
// Derived, Tuned, Resolution, Unknown (`src/provenance.rs`); a value without one does not load.
(
    crew_hp: (30, Tuned("owner decision 2026-10-23, kept 2026-10-28 (#104), provisional: one pool
        for every crew station of every tank, revised if play shows it out of proportion to the
        tank's other pools. Crew is one shared entity across tanks, and the pool has no relation to
        the crew box's size. The field's calibration in spall_cone.ron and the crew line rate in
        the round files (assets/rounds/) are set against it")),
)
